  "text": "DONE. The simulation now passes (1 test passed under Icarus). I did not run lint, `check` or the Verilator run after the change.\n\nThe cause was `ph`, the 3-bit phase counter in `rtl/soak_core.sv` that aligns the snapshot request. It was never reset, so it stayed X in simulation. That kept the snapshot from ever completing, and the counters read 0 in the failing tests. I added `ph <= 3'd0;` to the reset branch, which is the only change."
